{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "07ZM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}' \\subset \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-sections-annihilated-by-ideal}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-subsheaf-sections-annihilated-by-ideal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e52fedfdd66443bdb2d28e2c2a1f597b82dbb55aa488003527613868af24b178", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d4fe4365aba059fa90c9098b84d56603066cf81619d14553e60483753e8af8ad", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals\nof finite type.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0004>-module.\nThe subsheaf <MATH_0005> defined in\nLemma <REF_0001> above is called\nthe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>subsheaf of sections annihilated by <MATH_0006><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b211d61e07cc4ecbae45600cd5f8633b71bfe283ba716fe2c80a582da2e2e27", "unit_id": "tag:01PP:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07ZM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}' \\subset \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{I}\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}' \\subset f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{I}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-push-sections-annihilated-by-ideal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b6e8d346e12d319bbce0d0d2416469a7f45845635a210b758c8006ea715d6ffa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:397dd1127e5f181be3d0ae105a97cf39ae6a5f2b2f89dd1c30eec782a1ec607c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism\nof schemes. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent\nsheaf of ideals of finite type. Let <MATH_0003> be a quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0004>-module. Let <MATH_0005>\nbe the subsheaf of sections annihilated by <MATH_0006>.\nThen <MATH_0007> is the subsheaf\nof sections annihilated by <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8e0b238c58129731bec6847a81e7d0a55973fbc1d9fda481bdb06b1b1663674c", "unit_id": "tag:07ZN:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07ZM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0004": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-sections-annihilated-by-ideal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a74b94dfd774ca6393bbd002b5565440917ed19daf179ed2d1337fa893651717", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:51d2c4f0036f010aec30597055e9853ddd2185b774e3152ddb20c47623b025a1", "source_text": "Omitted. (Hint: The assumption that <MATH_0001> is quasi-compact and\nquasi-separated implies that <MATH_0002> is quasi-coherent\nso that Lemma <REF_0001> applies\nto <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004>.)\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d681725077a74e10d825c7da2dc01d2c07237218d3b2ceeb8a2c04af808c76fd", "unit_id": "tag:07ZN:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07ZM", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-remark-sections-support-in-closed}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a50a54f66a1cfec859638e1eae170c024640daf6980cb5e2e7991dc03b5ebe9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFor an abelian sheaf on a topological space we have discussed the subsheaf\nof sections with support in a closed subset in\nModules, Remark <REF_0001>.\nFor quasi-coherent modules this submodule isn't always a quasi-coherent\nmodule, but if the closed subset has a retrocompact complement, then\nit is.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b520224705ef76cc4a6c15f5c0beec19cca59313130e70463a6aa510f6c6dbee", "unit_id": "tag:07ZM:prose-0002"}
